  "id": "Compound::DB00528 - Gene::1576",
  "verbalization": "Lercanidipine is likely to interact with Cyp3a4 through a series of molecular and enzymatic pathways. The evidence suggests that Lercanidipine binds to Cyp3a7, which then participates in multiple enzymatic activities, including oxidoreduction and oxygen binding. These activities are all mediated by Cyp3a4, indicating a potential functional link between Lercanidipine and Cyp3a4. The shared participation in these processes implies that Lercanidipine may influence Cyp3a4 through its interaction with Cyp3a7, possibly by modulating the activity of the enzyme complex. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which Lercanidipine affects Cyp3a4, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
